WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.576
Magrib paced back and forth in the hot sun.

2
00:00:18.577 --> 00:00:22.076
He did not hear Aladdin's call for help.

3
00:00:22.077 --> 00:00:26.571
He was thinking about the lamp and making big plans.

4
00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:33.929
"Soon I will be richer than any king!" he said with an evil grin.

5
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.617
"I will be the most powerful man on earth!"

6
00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:45.962
Magrib laughed and did a merry little dance.

7
00:00:45.963 --> 00:00:48.889
Then he stopped and frowned.

8
00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.920
"Where is that boy?

9
00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:53.536
He has been gone too long."

10
00:00:53.537 --> 00:00:56.349
Suddenly Magrib touched his ear.

11
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.948
Had he heard something?

12
00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.280
"Uncle! I am back!

13
00:01:01.281 --> 00:01:02.541
Can you hear me?"

14
00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:05.286
It was Aladdin calling again.

15
00:01:05.287 --> 00:01:09.953
Magrib ran to the opening in the earth and looked over the edge.

16
00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:11.917
"What are you doing, boy?

17
00:01:11.918 --> 00:01:14.764
Come up right now!"

18
00:01:14.765 --> 00:01:18.070
"Uncle, I cannot," answered Aladdin.

19
00:01:18.071 --> 00:01:20.805
"I am too heavy to climb this last step.

20
00:01:20.806 --> 00:01:24.466
My pockets are full and my jacket is bulging.

21
00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.780
I am carrying many pieces of glass fruit from the garden.

22
00:01:27.781 --> 00:01:30.557
Please help me up!"

23
00:01:30.558 --> 00:01:34.866
"Just give me the lamp, boy," snapped Magrib.

24
00:01:34.867 --> 00:01:37.962
"It is the lamp that weighs you down.

25
00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:41.959
Give me the lamp and your load will be lighter."

26
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.160
"The lamp? Oh yes, the lamp.

27
00:01:44.161 --> 00:01:46.736
I have it here someplace.

28
00:01:46.737 --> 00:01:49.271
But, Uncle, it is not the lamp that weighs me down.

29
00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:51.695
The lamp is not heavy."

30
00:01:51.696 --> 00:01:55.489
"Where is the lamp?" asked Magrib eagerly.

31
00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.934
"What have you done with it?"

32
00:01:57.935 --> 00:02:02.212
"It's wrapped in my sash in my back pocket," said Aladdin.

33
00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:04.739
"I will gladly give it to you when I get up there.

34
00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.024
Please give me a hand!"

35
00:02:07.025 --> 00:02:12.795
"Just give me the lamp, boy!" the magician shouted angrily.

36
00:02:12.796 --> 00:02:16.696
"I cannot reach the lamp," said Aladdin. "See?"

37
00:02:16.697 --> 00:02:19.742
He stretched his arm toward his back.

38
00:02:19.743 --> 00:02:21.732
"I am loaded with glass fruit.

39
00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:23.545
They are for my mother."

40
00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:25.754
He reached into a pocket.

41
00:02:25.755 --> 00:02:27.609
"Here is a sparkling red one.

42
00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.929
You may have it!"

43
00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.981
"No!" screamed Magrib.

44
00:02:32.982 --> 00:02:35.031
"I don't want any jewels!

45
00:02:35.032 --> 00:02:36.795
I want only the lamp!

46
00:02:36.796 --> 00:02:39.500
Give it to me now! NOW!"

47
00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.821
"I will, Uncle, I promise," said Aladdin firmly.

48
00:02:42.822 --> 00:02:45.697
"But I cannot give it to you yet."

49
00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:50.655
Magrib leaned down so that Aladdin could see his angry face.

50
00:02:50.656 --> 00:02:54.095
His cheeks were a terrible shade of red.

51
00:02:54.096 --> 00:02:59.593
"You refuse to obey me?" hissed the magician.

52
00:02:59.594 --> 00:03:03.803
"I cannot obey you," said Aladdin. "I―"

53
00:03:03.804 --> 00:03:09.381
Magrib threw back his head and screamed, "You cannot obey?"

54
00:03:09.382 --> 00:03:14.080
The magician stomped his feet until dust flew up around him.

55
00:03:14.081 --> 00:03:17.003
He pounded his head with his fists.

56
00:03:17.004 --> 00:03:21.553
"Cannot obey me?" he screamed.

57
00:03:21.554 --> 00:03:25.340
He pulled the silver box from his sleeve.

58
00:03:25.341 --> 00:03:28.629
"Will not obey ME?"

59
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:34.160
Magrib grabbed a handful of the powder and muttered some magic words.

60
00:03:34.161 --> 00:03:38.524
"You will be sorry, you worthless boy!"

61
00:03:38.525 --> 00:03:42.618
"What are you doing, Uncle?" cried Aladdin. "Help me!"

62
00:03:42.619 --> 00:03:47.363
Magrib threw the powder onto the glowing ashes of the fire.

63
00:03:47.364 --> 00:03:51.294
Flames shot into the air, higher than his head.

64
00:03:51.295 --> 00:03:56.642
"No, my boy, now you will never get out!" he screamed.

65
00:03:56.643 --> 00:04:01.885
"Uncle!" Once again, the ground shook.

66
00:04:01.886 --> 00:04:07.685
From the stone steps, Aladdin saw the marble door start to close over his head.

67
00:04:07.686 --> 00:04:11.928
The door to the enchanted treasury fell back into place.

68
00:04:11.929 --> 00:04:17.341
Then rocks and dirt rolled down and covered it completely.

69
00:04:17.342 --> 00:04:22.427
Magrib shook his fists at the sky and twisted his body in fury.

70
00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:28.013
"Aaaaargh!" he groaned. "Everything is ruined!"

71
00:04:28.014 --> 00:04:33.693
"Uncle!" Aladdin shouted into the darkness. "UNCLE!"

72
00:04:33.694 --> 00:04:35.289
No one heard him.

73
00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:40.158
No one answered.
